{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And the priest who offers the burnt-offering of a man.</b> One should not interpret this to mean specifically the priest who offers it, thereby excluding the rest of the priests from having a share in it, for this expression is like the expression of the verse above, ״הכהן המחטא אותה יאכלנה״ — 'the priest who purifies it shall eat it' — where the intent is not to exclude the rest of the priests. Rather, it says 'the priest who offers' to say that whoever is fit to offer has a share in the skin, to exclude the impure one, who is not fit to offer and has no share in it. And what the verse added by saying ״אשר הקריב״ — 'that he offered' — means that he has already offered it, and it comes to clarify that when the verse grants the priest the skin of the burnt-offering, this is after it has been offered upon the altar and its owners have fulfilled their obligation through its offering; but if it was slaughtered and found to be a טרפה, or its blood was spilled and not cast as required, the verse does not grant him the skin. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted that all the offerings were inspected before their offering, so that they would not offer a טרפה upon the altar — for the priests would inspect the טרפה with the seven inspections of the eye and with other signs before slaughter — and therefore it added ״אשר הקריב״, meaning that it has already counted for him as an offering."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:23:42.201322606Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}